[36m(PPOTrainer pid=3924694)[0m INFO 04-13 01:47:15 ppo_trainer.py:897] [trace] step=35 reward=-0.700 response_len=3956 completion_len=7299 total_len=8192 preview='systemYou are ChatGPT, a large language model trained by OpenAI.\\nKnowledge cutoff: 2024-06\\nCurrent date: 2026-04-13\\n\\nReasoning: medium\\n\\n# Valid channels: analysis, commentary, final. Channel must be included for every message.\\nCalls to these tools must go to the commentary channel: \'functions\'.developer# Instructions\\n\\nYou are a chemist analyzing drug molecules. Available features for the get_features and get_neighbors tools: molecular_weight, heavy_atom_count, heteroatom_count, logp, tpsa, h_bond_donors, h_bond_acceptors, rotatable_bonds, fraction_csp3, molar_refractivity, complexity, electronic, functional_groups, ring_systems, 3d_properties, structural_alerts, metabolites, pka, ionization, logd, solubility\\n\\n# Tools\\n\\n## functions\\n\\nnamespace functions {\\n\\n// Compute selected molecular features for a given SMILES string. Pass a list of feature names to select which analyses to run.\\ntype get_features = (_: {\\n// Input molecule as a SMILES string.\\nsmiles: string,\\n// List of feature categories to compute.\\nfeature_names: string[]\\n}) => any;\\n\\n// Find nearest neighbors from the PAMPA_NCATS training set with labels, similarity scores, and optionally compute selected molecular features for each neighbor.\\ntype get_neighbors_pampa = (_: {\\n// Input molecule as a SMILES string.\\nsmiles: string,\\n// Optional list of feature categories to compute for each neighbor.\\nfeature_names?: string[],\\n// Number of nearest neighbors to return. Default 5.\\nnum_neighbors?: number,\\n// Whether to include task labels for neighbors. Default true.\\ninclude_labels?: boolean\\n}) => any;\\n\\n} // namespace functionsuserInstructions: Answer the following question about drug properties.\\nContext: Membrane permeability is a measure of the ability of a drug to pass through a cellular membrane through passive diffusion, which is necessary for the drug to affect a cell. In general, small hydrophobic drugs can easily pass through membranes whereas large polar/charged drugs do not easily pass through. PAMPA (parallel artificial membrane permeability assay) is a commonly employed non-cell-based assay to evaluate drug permeability across the cellular membrane.\\nQuestion: Given a drug SMILES string, predict whether it\\n(A) is not permeable to cell membranes in a PAMPA assay (B) is permeable to cell membranes in a PAMPA assay\\nDrug SMILES: CC1=CC(=CC(=C1)C2=NC3=C(O2)C=C(C=C3)C4=C(C(=C(C=C4)OC)OC)OC)C\\nAnswer:\\nPlease think step by step and use the relevant tools in your analysis. Then put your final choice, (A) or (B), after "Answer:"assistantanalysisWe need to analyze drug properties and predict whether it is permeable or not in PAMPA. We are given a drug SMILES string: "CC1=CC(=CC(=C1)C2=NC3=C(O2)C=C(C=C3)C4=C(C(=C(C=C4)OC)OC)OC)C"\\n\\nWe must decide if it\'s permeable. We\'ll use get_neighbors_pampa function: we input SMILES, optional feature_names, default 5 neighbors, include labels.\\n\\nAlternatively we can get features (molecular_weight, logp, tpsa, rotatable_bonds, etc.) to help.\\n\\nUse get_neighbors_pampa to see nearest neighbors in PAMPA dataset, and check label of permeability? The function returns nearest neighbors with labels? The include_labels is default true. So get_neighbors_pampa returns neighbors with similarity scores and labels. Let\'s call it.\\n\\nAlso maybe get_features for features.\\n\\nWe should use these.assistantcommentary to=functions.get_neighbors_pampa json{"smiles":"CC1=CC(=CC(=C1)C2=NC3=C(O2)C=C(C=C3)C4=C(C(=C(C=C4)OC)OC)OC)C","num_neighbors":5}functions.get_neighbors_pampa to=assistantcommentary{"result": "Nearest Neighbors for task \'PAMPA_NCATS\' (k=5):\\n\\n1. COC1=C(C(=C(C=C1)C2=CC3=C(C=C2)N=C(O3)C4=CC=C(C=C4)SC)OC)OC (similarity: 0.7417, label: A)\\n\\n2. CC1=CC=CC=C1C2=NC3=C(O2)C=C(C=C3)C4=C(C(=C(